; The shield (issue #275): a broad defensive head that blocks hits and knocks
; attackers back. Low damage output focused on control through knockback.
;
; A large flat head, 56 px wide and 32 px tall, designed to intercept incoming
; attacks. It swings slowly (drive 24 rad/s, extend 600 px/s) but has enough
; mass to hold a position and deflect. The head is twelve circles arranged in
; a grid to cover the broad face, allowing it to block multiple simultaneous
; strikes. Low damage (20) encourages using it for control rather than kills;
; knockback is moderate (same force ceiling as the pickaxe, 8000) so a
; well-planted shield stops lighter attacks cold.
;
; Reach M (140 px) like the pickaxe to keep the broad head manageable. Heavy
; mass (0.4) makes it slow but stable. Force ceiling 8000, but the heavy weight
; and slow responsiveness make it feel heavier than weapons with that cap.

[resource]
